# Alpha Admin design system (agents)

Canonical product write-up: `../alpha-docs/ADR-shared-design-system.md` (esp. §3 / §3b).

## Accent

- Accent is a **whisper** for checks, sparse marks, focus — **not** selected cards, section rows, FABs, body text, or primary CTAs.
- Never paint selected Settings cards / list rows with accent border or accent wash. Use grayscale fill (`--fg-4` / `--fg-8`).

## Icons

- Prefer existing icons: `Pen`, `Share` (filled), `Crown`, `Trash`, `NavIcon`, `@alpha/ui` SVGs.
- Do **not** invent inline person/share glyphs when a product icon exists.
- Icon color on quiet chrome: `currentColor` at `--fg-66`, not full ink.

## Buttons

- Default chrome actions: **pill / round** with subtle `--fg-8` background, no heavy stroke.
- Avoid stroked rectangular buttons inside cards.
- Primary CTAs: ink-on-bg (existing `--button-primary-*`), not accent-filled.

## Destructive

- Disconnect, Delete, cancel-danger: **grayscale only** (muted text + quiet fill).
- Never use `--destructive` rose, `--accent-2`, or `--accent-3` for these.

## Settings profiles

- No duplicate “Profiles” header under the shell Settings title.
- Admin = **crown** beside name; do not print owner/admin/member labels on cards.
- Selected card slightly larger; same subtle stroke as unselected + Add Profile.
- Add Profile: horizontal row, fatter stroked `+` circle, larger plus.
- Active card actions: round icon pills (Pen, filled Share) — not text CTAs.
